SUSPECTED BUG: end to end (large, -fanout=2). retry.Do over txm.WithTx over a closure calling execute; the result is
wrapped "transfer %d: %w", an audit failure is joined, the success path ends in bus.Notify, which swallows
everything. Correct set: execute's set behind "transfer %d: %w" (also joined with rollback errors), Begin errors
behind "tx: begin: %w", ErrGaveUp, ctx errors behind "retry: interrupted: %w", each with and without errors.Join;
audit.ErrClosed/ErrFull/write errors behind errors.Join; NO event-handler origin.
Actual: no event-handler origin (good), but (1) execute's errors are missing (only WithTx's unresolved values,
plan S08, see tx_withtx_decl); (2) the errors of other callers' retry closures appear (NotFoundError, filerepo read
errors, errDryRun via probe$2; plan S09); (3) errors.Join(err, aerr) makes one value per combination of its
operands' values (about 50 x 25), which exceeds the cap of 1024: the result is cut, with an
unresolved(fixpoint-limit) entry, and every entry without errors.Join (the plain "return err" path) and the
"retry: interrupted: %w" entries are gone.
-- args --
-fanout=2 service/service.go:@transfer
